# Keys and anything holding one. A private key reaching a public repository is
# unrecoverable — the key is spent the moment it is pushed — so these are
# matched broadly rather than exactly.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*-keypair.json
keeper/.agent/
REBUILD.md
Problems.md

# Planning documents are working notes, not the product. MASTERPLAN.md also
# names the pre-IPO issuers this entry refused, and `scripts/eligibility.mjs`
# fails any tracked file that does — which is the rule working, not a reason
# to weaken it.
MASTERPLAN.md
frontendplan.md

# The collector's store. 14MB and growing, rebuildable from `--backfill` plus
# a catch-up pass, and it is a working set rather than a source: committing it
# would put a binary in every diff for data the chain and the API still hold.
data/collector.db
data/collector.db-wal
data/collector.db-shm

# The same reasoning for the cost-of-the-night study and the bell poster's
# audit log: working sets on this machine, summarised into tracked JSON.
data/night-cost.db
data/night-cost.db-wal
data/night-cost.db-shm
data/bell-poster.db
data/bell-poster.db-wal
data/bell-poster.db-shm

# Crates outside the workspace build into their own target directories, and
# the Pyth Lazer binary the integration harness loads is fetched from mainnet
# by `tests/integration/fetch.sh` rather than committed.
tests/integration/target/
tests/integration/fixtures/*.so
tools/*/target/
